#
# A Ray class is Julia's own: an abstract type carries the inheritance (`AbstractHole <: AbstractSource`), a
# mutable struct is the class (`Hole <: AbstractHole`), a field is a struct field read through a function of the
# same name (`mass(h)`, its default made on first read), and every member is a function dispatched on the abstract
# type - multiple dispatch finds the nearest class, as Ray's chain does. `@class` (below) lays a class out; the
# Ray-facing functions and operators are in `Rt.Ops`. Numbers are Float64, lists Vector{Any} (`List`).
