"""
    @class Name <: Parent begin ... end

A Ray class: an abstract type under the parent's (`AbstractName <: AbstractParent`), a mutable struct holding the
fields of the class and of every parent, a function per field (its default made on first read), and every member
written in the body - `function f(self::__class__, ...)` - dispatched on the abstract type, so a subclass takes
what it does not redefine. `self::Type{<:__class__}` is a static. A member no class of a value has is found by
name (`Rt.dyn`): in a `Node`, in the slots Ray set on an object, or elementwise on a `Many`.
